devx-maria: Kicking off a targeted quickstart refresh — scope: auth flow, first-deploy steps, and updating code snippets to SDK v5. Goal is minimal friction for new devs.

kai: Nice. Can we make the ephemeral example use fetch + server endpoint pattern? avoids exposing long-lived keys.

devx-maria: Yes. Draft snippet in PR uses a tiny server exchange. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/starterkit/pull/341 (docs-only). Files touched: quickstart.md, docs/auth.md, examples/ephemeral.md

amy: I'll check the SDK snippets for idiomatic v5 usage. also flagging one broken link in quickstart to the deploy checklist.

ben: Heads-up from infra: recommend ephemeral TTL=10m for demos. examples can show 5m but call out tradeoffs.

devx-maria: noted — updated auth.md with guidance and sample env usage: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY on server. Snippet:
```
// server: /api/ephemeral
const r = await fetch('https://api.redwood-inference.dev/ephemeral', {
  method: 'POST',
  headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY}` }
});
const { ephemeral_key } = await r.json();
// client
const client = new RedwoodClient({ apiKey: ephemeral_key });
```

amy: tiny wording nit: replace "instantiate" with "initialize" in quickstart line ~52.

devx-maria: fixed. Also added a short "what changed" note at top so returning readers notice.

doc-bot: PR 341 lint: 1 warning (style) — https://ci.redwood-inference.dev/checks/341. Preview: https://docs-preview.redwood-inference.dev/starterkit/341

deploy-bot: preview live: https://deploy-preview-341--starterkit.netlify.app/quickstart

kai: one content ask: include a one-sentence rationale for server-side exchange in auth.md (security + revoke ability).

devx-maria: added rationale. Plan: merge tomorrow midday if no blockers. @amy please post any SDK wording changes before then.

amy: Will do. Left two small inline suggestions on the PR.

ben: LGTM from infra after TTL note.

devx-maria: Thanks folks — aiming to ship this as a small, safe docs refresh. :rocket:
